WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:04.890
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.310
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.170
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们一起演过《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.290
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你打造了终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

5
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.810
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们将通过独家采访，深入探索《办公室》的世界，

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.970
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
幕后花絮，还有许多闺蜜之间的故事。

7
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.010
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

8
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.000
Hi, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.000
Hi.
嗨。

10
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.280
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

11
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.760
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

12
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.020
We have all had a very eventful morning in our own ways today.
今天我们每个人都经历了一个相当多事的早晨。

13
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.860
We just had a clunky morning, didn't we?
我们的早晨过得有点手忙脚乱，对吧？

14
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.700
I mean, Sam has the craziest story.
我是说，萨姆有个最疯狂的故事。

15
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.200
Yeah, Sam, I think you win.
对，萨姆，我觉得你赢了。

16
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:42.600
Yeah.
对。

17
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.220
Someone stole my laundry.
有人偷了我的衣服。

18
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:45.340
What the heck?
搞什么鬼？

19
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:51.140
Someone stole my clean, dry laundry out of the machine and my laundry basket out of the laundry.
有人把洗衣机里我洗净烘干的衣服和我的洗衣篮一起偷走了。

20
00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:51.940
And your basket.
连你的篮子一起。

21
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.980
I didn't know that part.
我之前不知道这部分。

22
00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.180
That's how I know it's on purpose.
所以我才知道这是故意的。

23
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.760
It's someone that is intentionally stealing it.
这是有人蓄意偷窃。

24
00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.560
This is a premeditated laundry thievery.
这是一场有预谋的偷衣贼行径。

25
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.780
I needed those clothes, too.
我那些衣服我也很需要啊。

26
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.300
This is within your building.
这是在你们大楼里发生的。

27
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:02.720
Yeah.
对。

28
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.300
So this, right.
所以这个嘛，没错。

29
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.380
So what is the plan here?
那接下来的计划是什么？

30
00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.500
And is this a case for mom detectives?
这算不算是妈妈侦探的案子？

31
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.020
And are there any cameras?
有什么摄像头吗？

32
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:10.720
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

33
00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:11.400
I need your help.
我需要你们的帮助。

34
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.120
What type of note do I put up?
我该贴一张什么类型的字条上去？

35
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.340
I need it because I need it to be aggressive, but I also need it to be passive.
我需要它语气强硬一点，但也得带点被动攻击。

36
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.800
I will help you.
我来帮你。

37
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.840
Well, Jenna can do the aggressive and I'll do the snark.
珍娜负责强硬，我负责讽刺。

38
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:22.620
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

39
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.420
And we'll compose this note.
我们就来写这张字条。

40
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.000
Yeah.
对。

41
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.800
You want to start it off, Jenna?
珍娜，你想开头吗？

42
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.240
My first thought is that you come in strong and you open with something like, to the laundry thief.
我的第一想法是你开门见山，用类似“致偷衣贼”这样的话开头。

43
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.380
Okay.
好的。

44
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.100
But now I'm wondering about that.
但现在我在琢磨这样行不行。

45
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.920
Is that the right move?
这招对吗？

46
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:38.960
Where does that end, though?
不过这样写会发展到哪一步呢？

47
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.060
Like, meet me outside?
比如，有种“有本事外面单挑”的感觉？

48
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.880
It's sort of like, I would really like my laundry back.
感觉就像是，我真的很想把我的衣服要回来。

49
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.320
Okay.
好吧。

50
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.740
No questions asked.
既往不咎。

51
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.200
Please put it back in the laundry room along with my laundry basket.
请把它和我的洗衣篮一起放回洗衣房里。

52
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:51.880
Okay.
好的。

53
00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.580
I might start it also something like this.
我可能也会写成类似这样的开头。

54
00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:06.980
On Thursday, September 3rd, at whatever time it was, my entire clean laundry and my laundry basket were stolen or taken out of this room.
在9月3日星期四，不管那是几点，我整整一篮干净的衣服连同洗衣篮一起从这个房间被偷走或拿走了。

55
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:07.460
Okay.
好吧。

56
00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.460
Went missing.
不见了。

57
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.260
Went missing.
不见了。

58
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.720
I would very much like my clothes back and the laundry basket.
我非常希望能拿回我的衣服和洗衣篮。

59
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.360
No questions asked.
既往不咎。

60
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.340
Please leave them here.
请把它们留在这里。

61
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.560
If not, I will start asking around.
如果不这样，我就会开始四处打听。

62
00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.240
I will notice if you're wearing my clothes.
要是你穿着我的衣服，我一眼就能看出来。

63
00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.040
Can I post a picture of you two?
我可以发一张你们两个人的照片吗？

64
00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.860
If not, I will get these two involved.
如果不的话，我就会把这两位牵扯进来了。

65
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:26.580
Yes.
可以。

66
00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.820
If that's what you want.
如果你想要这样的话。

67
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:28.720
Yes.
好。

68
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:36.800
I mean, that might be a bad idea because we do not have a great reputation for solving cases.
我的意思是，那或许是个馊主意，因为我们在破案这方面实在没什么好名声。

69
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.740
This is true, Sam.
确实如此，萨姆。

70
00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:38.900
We will have snacks.
我们会准备零食的。

71
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.240
We'll never find your clothes.
我们永远也找不到你的衣服。

72
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:40.860
True, true, true, true.
没错，没错，没错，没错。

73
00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.380
Yeah.
行吧。

74
00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.300
Ooh, can we stake out his laundry room with some snacks?
哦，我们可以带着零食去他的洗衣房外蹲守吗？

75
00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.680
This is becoming a slumber party so faSt.
这简直快变成睡衣派对了好吗。

76
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.800
If we're going to do that, we might as well watch Lord of the Rings.
既然我们要这么做，那干脆顺便把《指环王》看了吧。

77
00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.380
All three Lord of the Rings.
把《指环王》三部曲全看完。

78
00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.420
No, here's what we do.
不，我们这样办。

79
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.180
Get pizzas, yeah.
买点披萨，对。

80
00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:54.660
Yes.
行。

81
00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:01.640
Here's what we do is we get some nice clean laundry and a nice new basket and we just leave it there.
我们的做法是买一些漂漂亮亮的新衣服和一个崭新的篮子，然后直接把它放在那儿。

82
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.480
And set a trap?
然后设下陷阱？

83
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.440
And set a trap.
然后设下陷阱。

84
00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.200
And then we hide out in the bushes as we do.
接着我们就按老规矩躲进灌木丛里。

85
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:06.720
Yeah.
行。

86
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:06.920
Sure.
没问题。

87
00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.260
And we wait.
然后我们等待。

88
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.100
Stakeout style.
蹲守风格。

89
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:11.040
Great.
太好了。

90
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.380
I'm for this.
我赞成。

91
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:12.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

92
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:13.520
All right.
好吧。

93
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.120
All right.
好吧。

94
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.940
It is going to be weird, though, Sam.
不过，萨姆，这会很奇怪的。

95
00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.420
Like, I feel like your clothing is very uniquely you.
就好像，我觉得你的衣服非常有你的个人特色。

96
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.040
I know, yeah.
我也知道，对。

97
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.700
Someone got a bunch of sleeveless misfit shirts that they're not going to wear.
有人弄到了一堆根本不会穿的无袖非主流T恤。

98
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.200
Damn it.
该死。

99
00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.100
It's very strange.
这真的很奇怪。

100
00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:25.420
Yeah.
是啊。

101
00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.440
I mean, mine is lame in comparison.
我的跟这个比起来简直弱爆了。

102
00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.600
I just left the house kind of like in a rush and distracted and I didn't have my normal bag.
我出门时有点匆忙，而且心不在焉，没带我平时用的包。

103
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.080
You know how you pack your normal bag?
你知道你平时是怎么收拾包的吧？

104
00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.980
It was upstairs and I was rushing out.
它在楼上，而我当时正急着出门。

105
00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.420
I just grabbed a different bag, threw all my stuff in it.
我随便拿了另一个包，把所有东西都塞了进去。

106
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.280
And then I got in the car and I drove away.
然后我上车开走了。

107
00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.140
And I was like, wait, I don't have my laptop.
接着我就想，等等，我没带笔记本电脑。

108
00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.120
I don't have any of my things.
我什么东西都没带。

109
00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.140
And I had to drive back home.
我不得不开车回家。

110
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.480
I didn't take it out the door with me.
我根本没把它带出门。

111
00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:49.880
I don't know.
我也不知道。

112
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.620
And then Jenna, you had a total snafu.
然后珍娜，你遇到了一场彻底的混乱。

113
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.700
I spilled an entire cup of coffee all over my car.
我把整整一杯咖啡全洒在车里了。

114
00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:06.240
And when I texted the thread, Matt comes in hot and he's like, is this because you drink coffee out of a lidless ceramic mug?
当我把这事发到群里时，马特立刻气势汹汹地问，这是因为你用没有盖子的陶瓷马克杯喝咖啡吗？

115
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:06.900
Oh, yeah.
哦，对啊。

116
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.040
I was just connecting the dots.
我只是把这些线索串联起来。

117
00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.440
And I was like, no, this one actually had a cover.
然后我说，不对，这个其实是有盖子的。

118
00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.600
Meanwhile, Matt has been sick, but you're doing a little better.
与此同时，马特一直在生病，不过你现在好一些了。

119
00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.000
So we've had a wonky start this week.
所以我们这周开局有点波折。

120
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.120
But we're going to have a great episode.
但我们还是会有一期精彩的节目。

121
00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:27.120
Today's episode is a celebration of a few of the deep dives that we have taken on Office Ladies over the years.
今天的节目是为了庆祝我们在过去几年里对《办公室》进行的一些深度挖掘。

122
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.580
We get a lot of mail about our deep dives and we want to share a couple.
我们收到了很多关于深度挖掘的邮件，我们想分享其中几封。

123
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.300
The first one is from Dawn T.
第一封来自英属哥伦比亚省的唐·T.

124
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.240
in British Columbia, who said, I love your podcaSt.
她说，我太喜欢你们的播客了。

125
00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.820
I have listened to every episode and I am always so excited when new ones are released.
我听了每一期节目，每当新节目发布时我都兴奋不已。

126
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.540
Thank you for coming along with me on countless walks, drives, flights, etc.
谢谢你们陪伴我度过了无数次的散步、开车、航班等等。

127
00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:55.740
I have learned so much about my favorite show and also about so many other random fascinating things through all your deep dives and tangents.
通过你们所有的深度挖掘和闲聊，我不仅了解了我最喜欢的剧集，还学到了许多其他随机而迷人的知识。

128
00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.140
I could listen to you both all day.
我可以听你们俩聊上一整天。

129
00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.980
Dawn, I love that.
唐，我太喜欢这个了。

130
00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.640
Well, we also got this from Liz P.
嗯，我们还收到了来自田纳西州纳什维尔的莉兹·P.的邮件。

131
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.060
in Nashville, Tennessee.
莉兹说，嘿，办公室女士们，我是老听众了，第一次发邮件。

132
00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.820
Liz says, hey, Office Ladies, a long time listener, first time emailer.
我只想说，女士们，我真的超级爱你们。

133
00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.420
I'd just like to say that I absolutely love you, ladies.
我快要结束我的第三次重温了。

134
00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.260
I'm nearing the end of my third re-listen.
哦，天哪。

135
00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:15.280
Oh, my goodness.
太棒了。

136
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:16.300
Amazing.
哇。

137
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:16.820
Wow.
哇。

138
00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:23.960
And Liz goes on to say, from your deep dives to your soapboxes and everything in between, you ladies have taught me so much.
莉兹接着说，从你们的深度挖掘到你们的慷慨陈词以及介于两者之间的一切，女士们，你们教给了我太多东西。

139
00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.880
I love re-watching episodes with my boyfriend and telling him all the backstory that he didn't ask for.
我喜欢和男朋友一起重看剧集，并向他讲述他并没有要求的各种幕后故事。

140
00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:35.980
And then in parentheses, Liz says, he loves to hear it, though, because he's the Josh slash Lee to my Angela slash Jenna.
然后莉兹在括号里说，不过他很乐意听，因为他是我和安杰拉、珍娜对应的乔什或李。

141
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.840
Thank you so much for being a strong, empowering, safe place for me and so many others.
非常感谢你们成为我以及其他许多人坚强、赋能、安全的避风港。

142
00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.780
Love you, amazing ladies, so much.
非常爱你们，了不起的女士们。

143
00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.520
So we thought, why not revisit some of our favorite deep dives?
所以我们在想，为什么不重温一下我们最喜欢的深度挖掘呢？

144
00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.360
This is for all of y'all who love these.
这是送给所有喜欢这些内容的你们。

145
00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:57.400
And Angela, I know we got a letter from one listener who's wanted us to do this episode for a while now.
安杰拉，我知道我们收到了一位听众的信，他一直希望我们能做这样一期节目。

146
00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.200
Yes, Joshua S.
是的，来自加利福尼亚州洛杉矶的约书亚·S.

147
00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:07.380
from Los Angeles, California, wrote in and said, hey, ladies, I am married to one of you.
写信说，嘿，女士们，我娶了你们中的一员。

148
00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:12.720
And I've been saying for a really long time, will you please do the best of deep dives?
我很久以前就说过，你们能做一期最佳深度挖掘吗？

149
00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.260
I've literally said this for two years.
我真的说了两年了。

150
00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.780
And then some other people write in and you decide to do it.
然后其他人也写信来，你们就决定做了。

151
00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.620
Sincerely, longtime listener, Joshua S.
谨上，资深听众约书亚·S。

152
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.300
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

153
00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:28.380
I know.
我知道。

154
00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:33.060
And when we decided to do this, you said I told Josh we were going to do this.
当我们决定做这个的时候，你说过你告诉过乔希我们要这么做。

155
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.040
And he was like, wait, what?
然后他的反应是，等等，什么？

156
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:34.680
What?
什么？

157
00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.340
Because he has been saying this.
